# NOTE: this file is named `gitignore` (no dot) ON PURPOSE, and /new-project renames it to
# `.gitignore` when it copies the scaffold. A dotfile here would apply to base-template's OWN
# tree — its `/planning` rule would hide `scaffold/planning/` from base-template's git, so any
# NEW file added to the template's planning scaffold would be silently untracked. Already-tracked
# files keep working, which is what makes that failure quiet.
/target
**/target

# planning/ is a SYMLINK into the brain vault (core/_planning/<slug>) and is tracked by the
# agentic-portfolio (HQ) repo, NEVER by this one. Most repos scaffolded from this template are
# public; the vault is private. Without this rule the first `git add -A` commits the whole
# planning tree into the public repo.
/planning

# Nested planning/ dirs inside crates (knowledge.md, memory.md, archived SDLC worklogs).
**/planning/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.DS_Store
